I started playing Nethack a few years ago, generally without getting
far. I hadn't played for a long time until recently when I moved to
University and lost my internet connection, I started playing again.
After a couple of months work, here I am :)
I'd had a string of promising Valkyries that had got pretty deep
before YASD/YAADing, and I just decided to try a knight for a change.

The game was nothing out of the ordinary to start with, but I received
a wish from a grateful water demon while dipping for Excalibur. I got
+2 GDSM, which set me up for the early game. Found a spellbook on an
early level which I managed to read, turned out to be identify. I dove
down to Sokoban to get food, and came out with an "oR, plus some wands
and rings. I engrave-ID'd the wands but I don't think there was
anything useful.

Went back up to do the Mines, and found a (BoH on the way to town,
which helped me carry around armour to check at the altar. I also
found a couple of magic lamps, both blessed (even though one was in a
bones pile). The altar was crossaligned, so I B/U/C ID'd my kit and
and tried on my uncursed rings. My warhorse passed away when I was
playing with conflict to get some armour from the guards. Carried on
down to get the luckstone with no difficulties, and came back up. I
finally found a unicorn horn on the way.

I returned to the main branch and continued down. I managed to get
Excalibur just before I found my first altar. I got Grayswandir after
a bit of work, but decided to stick to a long sword for now as I
probably would have a low to hit with a saber at the moment.
Unfortunately I managed to lose it before I finally wanted to use it
:S

Somewhere along the line my rings got destroyed by a chest trap, but
the only one of any use was conflict, which I found again before going
into Hell.

The Quest was pretty easy, quasits are not very tough. But it was a
close call with Ixoth, being used to valkyries I didn't expect him to
be so tough. The Knight artifact doesn't seem that good though, unless
you're using magic a lot. I found a silver dagger inside though, which
I saved to #twoweapon with in hell.

On my way down I found a level with a couple of sinks on, so I kicked
them both until I got some succubi and danced to get me up to level
30. That was my main source of HP, except for a couple of short-lived
nurses.
I made a stash by an altar a few levels above Medusa, and found I
could now case identify with about 34% failure. I identified all my
kit, and started to enchant my armour. I found I had a =oTC so got
teleportitis at the next opportunity. I think at this point I used up
a magic lamp for a magic marker, to write ?oEA. I dumped the oil lamp
since I planned to keep the other magic lamp as a light source. I made
some !oHW and blessed the one ?oGenocide I found, to use on ;, and
uncursed some levitation boots I found. They turned out be -3, but
they got me across Medusa. I put on my blindfold and let my amulet do
the work. No shield on Perseus, but he had -1 levi boots so I dumped
my old ones and took them. I continued down till the castle, got the
wand and then came back up. I got 2 blessed scrolls of charging, to
use one on my magic marker, and enchanted my armour some more, and
Frost Brand a bit. I also got 2 blessed scrolls of genocide for L and
h (taking no chances).

I hunted out Ludios and cleared it out. I carefully ID'd all the
soldier's armour, but the best I got was a pair of +1 gloves. I took
all the cash down with me to the VotD, and bought some protection (I
lost this when I did #pray instead of #offer, but I got it back later
through prayer and a bit more money). I continued into Hell, making
sure to pick-axe a route between the stairs after I mapped each level.
When I found Vlad I took him out without any problems, and got the
"oLS (but didn't use it till the endgame). Orcus caused some trouble,
I had to use a /oDigging to escape to the next level, but he summoned
a named demon before I managed to get him to escape upstairs. I
managed to take out the demon, and then waited to regain some HP
before finishing Orcus. His wand was (0:2).
I continued down, and once I reached the bottom I marked the VS with
the candelabrum and went back up to my stash.

I did the same pick-axe job through the rest of the dungeon above,
before returning to my stash for some final sacrificing and holy
water. I decided to use the ?oEA I'd found to enchant up my shirt, but
inadvertently left my +5 speed boots on, which promptly vaporized. So,
I blew a wish on a new pair, plus some ?oCharging for my magic marker,
to enchant it back up. I left it at +4 this time, but wished for a
shield of relfection to use the remaining charges on. I wanted to be
able to wear a "oLS in the endgame, but still #twoweaponed through
most of hell.

Then I went down to see the wizard for the first time (this was only
my second time in hell, the first having died to brainlesness about 2
levels in). He went down easily enough, and I went down to do the
invocation. I cleared out the graveyard and fought through insects to
find the entrance to the high priest (using the bell). I used Orcus'
wand to kill him and waited a little to regenerate. I had saved a
c!oGL for this occasion, but decided I'd try and escape the hard way
and save that for later (I never did use it though). Again, I fought
throught the insects to make an easy path to the exit, and started the
final ascent.

The myserious force didn't kick in for a while, but once it started it
didn't stop. I had to deal with 17 Rodney's on the way back up. I also
lost a lot of luck when I tried to eat his corpse. I had to resume
eating a few times and didn't realise the cannibal penalty would kick
in again. I lost all my scrolls when I fell in a pool after forgetting
to put on my new =oLevitation. I dumped them all and carried on
regardless. Once I reached the VotD Rodney didn't show up again till
the endgame, so I reached the top without too much trouble. I
/oDeathed Rodney on the plane of Earth before he could double trouble,
but it took me a while to find the portal, by which time he had
appeared again. Fortunately some good came out of it, as the summoned
an Archon which I managed to tame using Charm Monster. He had
Demonbane, and luckily was next to me when I found the exit. Air
wasn't too much of a problem with the Archon at hand, but I stumbled
in to the exit without him. Fire and Water weren't a problem though.

I finally made it to Astral, and had to make do with my angel instead.
I decided to go for Famine first, as I had plenty of food. He went
down without touching me. Apart from the riders I fought little, using
a /oTele and a magic whistle, and making a path through insects again.
Unfortunately, it was the wrong altar, so I headed back to the start.
On the way my angel bit the dust, so I put on my =oConflict instead. I
took out Famine again on the way back, and headed for Pestilence. He
got me twice, but fortunately my unicorn horn (uncursed at this point,
I had run out of !oHW) saved me both times. Eventually I finished him
and made it to the altar, which was the correct one.


